The extensionPack Strategy (Recommended)

An extension can simultaneously act as a functional extension and an Extension Pack. By using the extensionPack property inside your package.json, you can auto-install recommended helper extensions while allowing users to manage them independently.
How it works:Installation: When a user installs your extension, VS Code automatically installs all extensions listed in the extensionPack.
Optional Behavior: Users are allowed to manually disable or uninstall the bundled pack extensions without breaking or uninstalling your main extension.

Configuration Example 

```
(package.json)json{
  "name": "my-main-extension",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "publisher": "my-username",
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.90.0"
  },
  "extensionPack": [
    "publisher.optional-helper-extension"
  ]
}

```

